vms-e839: alpha VMS -- the locals area must not overlap the arguments above it

alpha_vms_initial_elimination_offset puts the frame-pointer area (the
locals) at ALPHA_ROUND (sa_size + pv_save_size) above the stack pointer,
but computes the argument pointer -- and alpha_compute_frame_size the whole
frame -- from ALPHA_ROUND of the unrounded sum.  When sa_size + pv_save_size
is 8 mod 16 (a stack procedure saving FP, RA and PV: 24 bytes), the locals
start 8 bytes higher than the size budget allows for, so the last local
quadword overlaps the first quadword above the frame: for a varargs
function, the word the argument-home routine fills with the argument count.
At -O0 a function f (void *a, char *b, ...) keeps b in that word, and b
reads back as the argument count after OTS$HOME_ARGS.

Round the register-save area before adding the locals and pretend
arguments in both places, so the argument pointer and the frame size cover
the padding.

--- a/gcc/config/alpha/alpha.cc
+++ b/gcc/config/alpha/alpha.cc
@@ -7335,8 +7335,9 @@
   sa_size *= 8;
 
   if (TARGET_ABI_OPEN_VMS)
-    frame_size = ALPHA_ROUND (sa_size
-			      + (alpha_procedure_type == PT_STACK ? 8 : 0)
+    frame_size = ALPHA_ROUND (ALPHA_ROUND (sa_size
+					   + (alpha_procedure_type == PT_STACK
+					      ? 8 : 0))
 			      + frame_size
 			      + crtl->args.pretend_args_size);
   else
@@ -7478,7 +7479,7 @@
 	offset = ALPHA_ROUND (sa_size + pv_save_size);
 	break;
       case ARG_POINTER_REGNUM:
-	offset = (ALPHA_ROUND (sa_size + pv_save_size
+	offset = (ALPHA_ROUND (ALPHA_ROUND (sa_size + pv_save_size)
 			       + get_frame_size ()
 			       + crtl->args.pretend_args_size)
 		  - crtl->args.pretend_args_size);
